COMPOSITE

Problem:
Need to treat individual objects and groups of objects in the same way.
it's happened when we have composite objects (an object can contain type of itself like folder)

Core idea:
Organize objects into a tree structure where both single objects and collections share a common interface.
as "Component" interface
we use polymorphism and recursive logic

Roles:
Component: common interface for all objects
Leaf: individual object with no children
Composite: object that contains children
Client: works with Component without caring whether it is a Leaf or Composite

When to use:
when our domain need composite objects

