ADAPTER

Problem:
Need to use an existing class, but its interface is incompatible with what the client expects.
like we develop some image filter (and has related interface)
and simultaneously we want to use an external library (that has different interface)

Core idea:
Wrap the existing class and translate its interface into one the client can use.
like CaramelAdapter that accept external type, and map it to our internal type

Roles:
Target: the interface the client expects                        (internal interface)
Adaptee: the existing class with the incompatible interface     (external interface)
Adapter: converts Target calls into Adaptee calls               (middle class)
Client: uses the Target interface

When to use:
When you want to reuse an existing class without changing its code.

When not to use:
When you can directly modify the original class, or when too many layers of adaptation make the design unnecessarily complex.

