FLYWEIGHT

Problem:
Need to create a very large number of similar objects, but storing them separately uses too much memory.
like points on Maps

Core idea:
Share the common, immutable part of state between many objects, and keep only the unique part outside.
like icons

Note: we always need some factory class to ensure shared common is unique
      we use hashMap to guarantee

Roles:
Flyweight: shared object containing intrinsic state
ConcreteFlyweight: actual shared implementation
FlyweightFactory: creates and reuses flyweights
Client: supplies extrinsic state when using the flyweight
Types of state:

Intrinsic state: shared, common, immutable
Extrinsic state: unique, supplied from outside

When to use:
When you have huge numbers of fine-grained objects and memory usage is a problem.

