BRIDGE

Problem:
when we have a multi dimensional hierarchy
like a Messenger class that have some sub classes based on type (normal,secret,urgent,...)
and each type have some separate implementations (like telegram,whatsapp,...)


Core idea:
Split a class into two separate hierarchies:

Abstraction
Implementation and connect them with "composition" instead of inheritance.
connect to hierarchy by bridge (composition)

Roles:
Abstraction: high-level control interface                     (like secret,normal,)
RefinedAbstraction: extended versions of the abstraction
Implementor: interface for implementations                    (like telegram,..)
ConcreteImplementor: actual implementations

When to use:
When a class has multiple dimensions of change and inheritance would lead to too many subclasses.

When not to use:
When there is only one implementation, or when the added abstraction makes the design unnecessarily complicated.

