Problem:
Need to control access to an object without changing the object itself.
when we want hide the real obj, and guarantee to execute some logic
like logging, or lazy loading we put the main obj behind "proxy obj"

Core idea:
Create a placeholder or wrapper object that has the same interface as the real object and forwards requests to it, possibly adding control logic.


Roles:
Subject: common interface                 (for both real and proxy)
RealSubject: the actual object
Proxy: controls access to the real object
Client: uses Subject and may not know whether it talks to Proxy or RealSubject
Common uses:

Lazy loading
Access control
Logging
Caching
Remote access

When to use:
When you need an extra layer of control before reaching the real object.

When not to use:
When direct access is fine and the proxy only adds unnecessary complexity.

